+++ b/tools/wlcctrl/wlcctrl.1.scd
@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@ wlcctrl - A command line utility for kylin-wayland-compositor
 
 wlcctrl [command] [options...]
 
+# BEHAVIOR
+
+Commands are executed sequentially in the order they appear on the command line,
+so *--sleep* can be interleaved with any other command to orchestrate timing.
+
+*-l, --list*, *--outputs* and *--workspace* are regular commands executed in order.
+
+Execution stops at the first failing command and wlcctrl exits with a non-zero
+status; it exits with 0 only when every command succeeded.
+
 # GLOBAL OPTIONS
 
 *--help*
@@ -149,6 +159,11 @@ wlcctrl [command] [options...]
 
 # TOPLEVEL OPTIONS
 
+Window commands accept either a toplevel UUID or a name fragment.  A name
+fragment is matched case-insensitively against the window title, app ID and
+icon.  When a fragment matches more than one window, the command fails and
+the matching windows are listed by UUID.
+
 *-l, --list*
 	List the names of all known toplevel.
 
